    "id": "p7-ch15-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "A fair coin is tossed 5 times. What is the probability of getting 3 heads from the 5 tosses?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{5}{16}$",
      "worked": "Write H for heads and T for tails. The outcomes with exactly three heads are:\n\nHHHTT, HHTHT, HHTTH, HTHHT, HTHTH, HTTHH, THHHT, THHTH, THTHH, TTHHH.\n\nThere are 10 favourable outcomes. Each toss has two equally likely outcomes, giving $2^5=32$ equally likely sequences.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly 3 heads})&=\\frac{10}{32}\\\\P(\\text{exactly 3 heads})&=\\frac{5}{16}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
